WEBVTT

00:00:01.919 --> 00:00:05.377
As time passes,
a boy inevitably becomes a man

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:09.552
but what is not inevitable
is that a man become a warrior.

00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:12.221
A warrior must be forged,
like a sword

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:14.059
tempered by...

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:16.429
by...

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:20.330
tempered by experience.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.634
The path of a warrior
begins with...

00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:25.538
Alexander?

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:26.735
No! Wait!

00:00:32.582 --> 00:00:33.549
Sorry.

00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:35.414
I didn't mean to hit you.

00:00:41.024 --> 00:00:42.924
What is the meaning of this?

00:00:43.026 --> 00:00:44.323
I'm sorry.

00:00:44.361 --> 00:00:47.159
We made fullerenes
in chemistry class today

00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:49.165
and filled them with water.

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:50.928
I asked you to meet me here
after school.

00:00:51.034 --> 00:00:52.228
I have been waiting for you.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:54.134
I forgot.

00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:56.662
You forgot
because you allowed yourself

00:00:56.707 --> 00:00:58.675
to be distracted by foolishness.

00:00:58.709 --> 00:01:00.074
I'm sorry.

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.110
There is something
very important

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:07.116
I want to discuss with you.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.084
It concerns your future.

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:10.245
Sit.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.820
As time passes

00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:17.554
a boy inevitably becomes a man

00:01:17.594 --> 00:01:20.893
but what is not inevitable
is that a man becomes a sword.

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:22.660
What?

00:01:22.699 --> 00:01:25.395
No, I meant... warrior.

00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:28.131
The path of a warrior begins

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.537
with the First Rite
of Ascension.

00:01:30.574 --> 00:01:33.407
Is that when they hit you
with painstiks?

00:01:33.443 --> 00:01:35.343
No. No, that is the Second Rite.

00:01:35.379 --> 00:01:36.346
Oh.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.905
You are approaching
the Age of Ascension.

00:01:38.982 --> 00:01:41.280
It is time for you
to prepare for the ceremony.

00:01:41.318 --> 00:01:43.286
What do I have to do?

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.255
Well, your fighting skills
will be tested

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:49.918
and your knowledge
of the teachings of Kahless.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.552
It will be challenging

00:01:51.595 --> 00:01:54.564
but I will help you prepare.

00:01:54.598 --> 00:01:58.125
These are the kor'tova candles.

00:01:58.168 --> 00:02:00.602
They represent the fire
that burns

00:02:00.637 --> 00:02:02.730
within the heart
of a warrior.

00:02:02.773 --> 00:02:04.331
When you light yours

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.740
you will be declaring
your intention

00:02:06.777 --> 00:02:08.506
to become a warrior.

00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:10.843
Go ahead.

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:13.315
What if I don't want to?

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.818
If you do not participate
in the rite

00:02:15.852 --> 00:02:19.219
before the age of 13 years,
you will never be able

00:02:19.256 --> 00:02:21.451
to become
a true Klingon warrior.

00:02:21.491 --> 00:02:23.516
Well, I don't care about that.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.087
You may not care about it now,
but someday you might.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.598
Well, Mother always said that...
that I didn't have to do

00:02:29.633 --> 00:02:31.624
any of this Klingon stuff
if I didn't want to.

00:02:31.668 --> 00:02:34.831
It is your decision, but...

00:02:34.871 --> 00:02:36.031
Okay, then.

00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:37.563
I'm not going to do it.

00:02:37.607 --> 00:02:38.733
Alexander.

00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:41.744
You just said it was up to me.

00:02:41.778 --> 00:02:44.372
I don't want to be a warrior.

00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:24.652
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:24.687 --> 00:03:28.521
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:28.558 --> 00:03:30.526
Its continuing mission...

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.496
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.899
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:39.002 --> 00:03:43.496
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:40.828 --> 00:04:42.887
As a result, we won't
be able to rendezvous

00:04:42.964 --> 00:04:44.898
with the Kearsarge
for another four days.

00:04:44.999 --> 00:04:47.365
Will we be holding position
here until it arrives?

00:04:47.402 --> 00:04:48.835
Yes, and as it would seem

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.236
that we're in
for a relatively quiet time

00:04:51.272 --> 00:04:54.639
I shall use this opportunity
to visit the Hatarian system.

00:04:54.676 --> 00:04:57.804
There are some ancient ruins
that are just being excavated.

00:04:57.845 --> 00:04:59.335
The delay will also
make it possible

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.177
for Stellar Dynamics
to complete their study

00:05:01.215 --> 00:05:02.705
of the Vodrey Nebula.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.547
I'll let them know
that they can have

00:05:04.585 --> 00:05:06.519
more access
to the lateral sensor grid.

00:05:06.554 --> 00:05:08.181
We could use this time

00:05:08.222 --> 00:05:10.520
to recalibrate
the weapons targeting system.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.921
Mr. Worf?

00:05:15.897 --> 00:05:17.455
Yes, um...

00:05:17.498 --> 00:05:19.864
I will begin
the procedure immediately.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:22.199
Very good.

00:05:22.236 --> 00:05:23.601
Dismissed.

00:05:25.206 --> 00:05:26.673
Lieutenant?

00:05:26.708 --> 00:05:30.405
Could I have a word
with you for a moment?

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.747
I noticed several times
during the briefing

00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:38.547
that you appeared to be
a bit distracted.

00:05:38.586 --> 00:05:39.712
I apologize.

00:05:39.754 --> 00:05:41.881
In the future, I will make sure

00:05:41.923 --> 00:05:44.858
my personal affairs do not
interfere with my duties.

00:05:44.892 --> 00:05:46.792
Is everything all right?

00:05:48.296 --> 00:05:49.888
I'm having problems
with Alexander.

00:05:49.931 --> 00:05:52.559
He has made it clear he does
not wish to participate

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.295
in the First Rite of Ascension.

00:05:54.335 --> 00:05:57.236
Oh, I see.

00:05:57.271 --> 00:06:00.570
I tried to tell him
that it is an important part

00:06:00.608 --> 00:06:02.405
of a young Klingon's life

00:06:02.443 --> 00:06:04.502
but he does not understand.

00:06:04.545 --> 00:06:06.638
But he's had
so little opportunity

00:06:06.681 --> 00:06:08.512
to spend time with Klingons.

00:06:08.549 --> 00:06:11.518
You know, the Festival
of Kot'baval is tomorrow.

00:06:11.552 --> 00:06:14.146
If he could take part in that

00:06:14.188 --> 00:06:17.055
I'm sure he would
more fully appreciate

00:06:17.091 --> 00:06:19.252
what a rich cultural heritage
he comes from.

00:06:19.293 --> 00:06:23.627
There is the Klingon outpost
on Maranga IV.

00:06:23.664 --> 00:06:26.224
I'm sure they'll be
celebrating the festival.

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:27.427
Yes...

00:06:27.468 --> 00:06:29.197
but the outpost is
on the other side

00:06:29.237 --> 00:06:31.034
of the Vodrey Nebula.

00:06:31.072 --> 00:06:34.405
It would take three days
by shuttle to get there.

00:06:34.442 --> 00:06:35.704
Oh, the Enterprise
could be there

00:06:35.743 --> 00:06:37.301
in a fraction of the time
and still back

00:06:37.345 --> 00:06:38.972
in time for the rendezvous.

00:06:39.013 --> 00:06:40.480
Captain, I could not ask you...

00:06:40.515 --> 00:06:42.745
Mr. Worf, Stellar Dynamics
would like nothing better

00:06:42.784 --> 00:06:44.115
than a trip around the nebula.

00:06:44.152 --> 00:06:46.313
Thank you, sir.

00:06:57.398 --> 00:06:59.059
? Huya!?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.399
? eu-uh Ha', eu-uh Ha'!?

00:07:02.437 --> 00:07:04.496
? Ha'!?

00:07:04.539 --> 00:07:09.169
? nlka tai kai te-blah?

00:07:11.412 --> 00:07:16.111
? ni'tokor o-ta-ke ta Kor?

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:20.086
? Euh! YaH ki-tach cha'!?

00:07:20.121 --> 00:07:21.645
Bok'ta ku'mo.

00:07:24.125 --> 00:07:27.458
? ...ke'te Ha'?

00:07:27.495 --> 00:07:31.591
? ke euh kai ka chu'?

00:07:31.632 --> 00:07:34.829
? yaH ke'te cha'?

00:07:34.869 --> 00:07:36.496
? yaH!?

00:07:38.239 --> 00:07:40.207
? Ke le Qapla' tah!?

00:07:40.241 --> 00:07:43.335
? Ragateth bat'leth! Eh!?

00:07:43.377 --> 00:07:47.871
? yake euh Hiya keeu?

00:07:47.915 --> 00:07:49.610
? che yu?

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.551
? Euh! Ha'! Ha'!?

00:07:52.587 --> 00:07:54.248
? Ha'!?

00:07:55.990 --> 00:08:01.257
? Ragateth bat'leth...?

00:08:01.295 --> 00:08:03.991
Who's that?

00:08:04.031 --> 00:08:05.521
It is the tyrant Molor.

00:08:05.566 --> 00:08:08.865
He was so strong,
no one could stand against him.

00:08:10.505 --> 00:08:14.236
? nok'tar be'got
Hosh'ar te'not?

00:08:14.275 --> 00:08:17.039
What's he saying?

00:08:17.078 --> 00:08:18.705
He is asking if anyone else

00:08:18.746 --> 00:08:21.180
will have the courage
to stand up to Molor.

00:08:21.215 --> 00:08:24.912
? ...Hosh'ar te'not?

00:08:27.655 --> 00:08:31.216
? Kate Qapla' plakmara?

00:08:40.401 --> 00:08:42.665
? Ki'rok Molor?

00:08:42.703 --> 00:08:44.671
? Ki'rok?

00:08:44.705 --> 00:08:52.510
? ni'Kotor bak'to Ba'jak tu'mo?

00:09:01.989 --> 00:09:03.980
? O'tak tu'ro!?

00:09:21.242 --> 00:09:24.734
? nok'tar be'got?

00:09:24.779 --> 00:09:28.442
? Hosh'ar te'not??

00:09:46.901 --> 00:09:49.165
? Ki'rok, Molor! Ki'rok!?

00:09:49.203 --> 00:09:51.763
What is this?

00:10:09.924 --> 00:10:11.551
Jik'ta!

00:10:11.592 --> 00:10:13.287
You've wounded me!

00:10:17.298 --> 00:10:18.856
You fought well.

00:10:18.899 --> 00:10:20.230
What happens now?

00:10:20.268 --> 00:10:22.998
There is only one man
who can stand against Molor.

00:10:23.037 --> 00:10:25.528
? nik'tol Kahless...?

00:10:25.573 --> 00:10:27.734
It's Kahless.

00:10:27.775 --> 00:10:31.836
Kahless would rather die
than live under Molor's tyranny.

00:10:31.879 --> 00:10:34.939
? Molor gik'tal!?

00:10:44.325 --> 00:10:47.954
Ni'lot Kahless!

00:10:56.837 --> 00:10:59.203
Father...!

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.798
Where have you been?

00:11:00.841 --> 00:11:02.866
We were watching
the fire dancers.

00:11:02.977 --> 00:11:03.875
We?

00:11:03.978 --> 00:11:05.104
K'Nor and Bar'el.

00:11:05.146 --> 00:11:06.875
They live here on the outpost.

00:11:06.914 --> 00:11:07.881
I need some money.

00:11:07.915 --> 00:11:09.712
What for?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.048
Well, a man over there
says he has

00:11:12.086 --> 00:11:14.680
Molor's head in a box...
the real Molor.

00:11:14.722 --> 00:11:15.882
That is impossible.

00:11:15.923 --> 00:11:18.790
The real Molor died
centuries ago.

00:11:18.826 --> 00:11:19.986
I know... it's mummified.

00:11:20.027 --> 00:11:22.552
He offered to show us
for 50 darseks.

00:11:22.596 --> 00:11:25.292
He is trying to take your money.

00:11:25.333 --> 00:11:26.891
Please, Father, he's waiting.

00:11:26.934 --> 00:11:28.526
No, it is too late.

00:11:28.569 --> 00:11:29.729
We should go home.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:30.737
But I...

00:11:30.771 --> 00:11:32.238
Alexander, that is enough.

00:11:32.273 --> 00:11:33.240
Come.

00:11:33.274 --> 00:11:34.901
It is time to go.

00:11:34.942 --> 00:11:37.103
I have to say good-bye
to my friends.

00:11:37.144 --> 00:11:39.908
You can see your friends
again tomorrow.

00:11:39.947 --> 00:11:41.312
We're coming back?

00:11:41.349 --> 00:11:43.442
If you want to.

00:11:57.464 --> 00:11:58.453
Run, Alexander!

00:12:12.112 --> 00:12:14.012
Ni'tokor bak'to!

00:12:23.057 --> 00:12:24.991
K'pla, Worf.

00:12:25.025 --> 00:12:26.993
You were too much for them.

00:12:27.027 --> 00:12:29.655
I have seen you before.

00:12:29.697 --> 00:12:31.528
Who are you?

00:12:33.233 --> 00:12:34.564
A friend.

00:12:38.072 --> 00:12:39.539
You are K'mtar.

00:12:39.573 --> 00:12:42.474
Your brother sent me here
to protect you.

00:12:49.249 --> 00:12:51.547
He is gin'tak
to the House of Mogh.

00:12:51.585 --> 00:12:52.677
Gin'tak?

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.085
An adviser so trusted

00:12:54.121 --> 00:12:56.214
he has become
part of the family.

00:12:56.256 --> 00:12:58.850
Do you have any idea
who was behind the attack?

00:12:58.892 --> 00:13:01.190
It is a Klingon matter.

00:13:01.228 --> 00:13:02.820
It is not your concern.

00:13:02.863 --> 00:13:05.423
One of my officers
was almost killed.

00:13:05.466 --> 00:13:07.195
That makes it my concern.

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:12.035
Recently, rumors began
to circulate on the Homeworld

00:13:12.072 --> 00:13:15.371
that an assassination attempt
was going to be made

00:13:15.409 --> 00:13:16.876
on the family of Mogh.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:20.710
Kurn sent me here to make sure
nothing happened to Worf.

00:13:20.748 --> 00:13:23.239
Why didn't you warn him
before the attack was made?

00:13:23.283 --> 00:13:26.411
I tried to contact him
over subspace.

00:13:26.453 --> 00:13:28.751
I was told he was not aboard.

00:13:28.789 --> 00:13:31.758
I decided to beam directly
to the surface.

00:13:31.792 --> 00:13:33.783
And why didn't you
let us know about it?

00:13:33.827 --> 00:13:36.796
Forgive me for being blunt,
Commander

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.799
but when it comes
to protecting the house

00:13:39.833 --> 00:13:45.032
to which I have pledged my life,
I trust no one.

00:13:47.007 --> 00:13:48.804
I have full confidence

00:13:48.842 --> 00:13:51.606
in the officers
with whom I serve.

00:13:56.417 --> 00:13:59.147
One of the attackers
dropped this dagger.

00:13:59.186 --> 00:14:01.848
The design represents
the House of Duras.

00:14:01.889 --> 00:14:04.357
We have other evidence
that indicate

00:14:04.391 --> 00:14:06.859
the Duras sisters,
Lursa and B'Etor

00:14:06.927 --> 00:14:08.519
were behind the attack.

00:14:08.562 --> 00:14:11.030
What do you think
they were after?

00:14:11.064 --> 00:14:14.227
Kurn's seat on the Council,
of course.

00:14:14.268 --> 00:14:16.998
We cannot allow their attack
on our house to go unanswered.

00:14:17.037 --> 00:14:20.006
First, we must find them.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.531
At one point,
they were on Deep Space 9

00:14:22.576 --> 00:14:24.874
trying to sell
bilitrium explosives.

00:14:24.945 --> 00:14:27.038
That was months ago.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.049
No one knows
where they went from there.

00:14:30.083 --> 00:14:32.813
Maybe we can find them.

00:14:32.853 --> 00:14:35.151
We've arranged
for quarters on the ship

00:14:35.189 --> 00:14:36.315
if you'd like to stay.

00:14:36.356 --> 00:14:38.153
I would.

00:14:38.192 --> 00:14:41.252
Worf and I have much to discuss.

00:14:51.972 --> 00:14:54.873
I will send Kurn a message,
telling him what happened

00:14:54.908 --> 00:14:56.876
but he will not
receive it for days.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.707
He's gone
to the Hitora Colony...

00:14:58.745 --> 00:15:00.542
Why did you treat
Commander Riker

00:15:00.581 --> 00:15:01.605
so disrespectfully?

00:15:01.648 --> 00:15:03.138
You were rude.

00:15:05.686 --> 00:15:08.985
I may have been rude
by human standards.

00:15:09.022 --> 00:15:11.149
I meant no disrespect.

00:15:11.191 --> 00:15:14.854
What is the matter, Worf?

00:15:14.962 --> 00:15:18.693
Have you been living
so long among humans

00:15:18.732 --> 00:15:22.793
that you have forgotten
how Klingons behave?

00:15:22.836 --> 00:15:23.860
I have not forgotten.

00:15:23.971 --> 00:15:24.869
I'm merely stating

00:15:24.972 --> 00:15:27.065
that their ways are
different than ours.

00:15:27.107 --> 00:15:30.634
I trust you have made your son
aware of that fact, as well.

00:15:30.677 --> 00:15:32.042
Yes, of course I have.

00:15:32.079 --> 00:15:33.046
Good.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.640
Because someday, Alexander

00:15:35.682 --> 00:15:39.015
may be called upon
to lead the House of Mogh.

00:15:39.052 --> 00:15:41.680
Kurn has no male heir.

00:15:41.722 --> 00:15:43.553
He wants to make sure

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:46.684
that Alexander
is preparing himself.

00:15:46.727 --> 00:15:48.422
Does my brother doubt

00:15:48.462 --> 00:15:51.693
my ability to raise
my son as a Klingon?

00:15:51.732 --> 00:15:53.199
No

00:15:53.233 --> 00:15:56.862
but you are alone among humans.

00:15:56.904 --> 00:16:00.863
It cannot be easy
to keep our ways.

00:16:00.908 --> 00:16:03.035
No.

00:16:03.076 --> 00:16:04.475
It has not been easy.

00:16:04.511 --> 00:16:06.342
How are his fighting skills?

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:08.780
Can he handle a bat'leth?

00:16:08.815 --> 00:16:11.113
He is learning.

00:16:11.151 --> 00:16:13.415
He could be better.

00:16:15.022 --> 00:16:16.683
He must.

00:16:16.723 --> 00:16:19.692
He is nearing
the Age of Ascension.

00:16:19.726 --> 00:16:24.095
Actually, Alexander
has not yet committed himself

00:16:24.131 --> 00:16:26.224
to undergoing the rite.

00:16:26.266 --> 00:16:27.494
What?

00:16:27.534 --> 00:16:29.866
I have tried to explain to him

00:16:29.903 --> 00:16:31.461
how important it is

00:16:31.505 --> 00:16:34.235
but... he will not listen to me.

00:16:35.776 --> 00:16:39.007
Perhaps together...

00:16:39.046 --> 00:16:41.014
you and I...

00:16:41.048 --> 00:16:42.675
we can find a way

00:16:42.716 --> 00:16:46.618
to spark the boy's interest
in his heritage.

00:16:46.653 --> 00:16:50.020
I would be grateful
for any help you could offer.

00:16:50.057 --> 00:16:52.025
Tomorrow, then.

00:16:52.059 --> 00:16:53.720
Tomorrow.

00:16:55.228 --> 00:16:58.664
May I say good night to the boy?

00:16:58.699 --> 00:17:01.065
Yes, of course.

00:17:15.849 --> 00:17:17.646
Is this your mother?

00:17:17.684 --> 00:17:18.810
Yeah.

00:17:18.852 --> 00:17:21.047
She died when I was little.

00:17:24.191 --> 00:17:27.024
You miss her a great deal,
don't you?

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.654
It must be hard for you

00:17:29.696 --> 00:17:32.859
being the only Klingon
your age aboard this ship.

00:17:32.899 --> 00:17:34.867
Sometimes.

00:17:34.901 --> 00:17:37.734
Have you ever been
to the Homeworld?

00:17:37.771 --> 00:17:39.068
No.

00:17:39.106 --> 00:17:41.506
I think you would like it there.

00:17:41.541 --> 00:17:43.509
At your uncle's house,
there is a lake

00:17:43.543 --> 00:17:46.512
you can swim in that is so clear

00:17:46.546 --> 00:17:48.810
you can see all the way
to the bottom.

00:17:48.849 --> 00:17:49.816
Really?

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:52.011
Mm-hmm.
You have cousins there.

00:17:52.052 --> 00:17:53.679
They want to meet you.

00:17:55.455 --> 00:17:56.752
I don't know.

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.087
I understand.

00:17:58.125 --> 00:17:59.888
You're afraid.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.827
You don't know
whether the Homeworld is safe.

00:18:02.896 --> 00:18:04.830
Yeah.

00:18:04.931 --> 00:18:09.061
And what happened today
on the planet is frightening.

00:18:09.102 --> 00:18:10.831
You're still troubled.

00:18:10.871 --> 00:18:13.704
I thought they were going
to kill my father.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:18.006
You must have wanted
to help us fight them off.

00:18:18.045 --> 00:18:20.479
I didn't know what to do.

00:18:20.514 --> 00:18:23.506
Someday, if you work hard

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:28.647
you will become a warrior...
a Klingon warrior.

00:18:28.689 --> 00:18:31.157
And you will always feel safe

00:18:31.191 --> 00:18:34.183
because you will know
how to defend yourself.

00:18:34.227 --> 00:18:36.491
And I'll tell you
something else.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:40.432
If anyone ever tries to hurt
your father again

00:18:40.467 --> 00:18:43.766
you will be able to fight
at his side

00:18:43.804 --> 00:18:47.604
and make sure
nothing happens to him.

00:18:47.641 --> 00:18:50.610
What do you think of that?

00:18:53.013 --> 00:18:55.709
Good night, Alexander.

00:18:55.749 --> 00:18:57.717
Dream well.

00:18:57.751 --> 00:18:59.582
Good night, K'mtar.

00:19:22.442 --> 00:19:24.000
Any luck?

00:19:24.044 --> 00:19:26.171
Starfleet records
contain no mention

00:19:26.213 --> 00:19:29.842
of the Duras sisters after their
departure from Deep Space 9.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:33.317
Did I not tell you as much?

00:19:33.353 --> 00:19:35.548
Have you been able
to contact Deep Space 9?

00:19:35.589 --> 00:19:38.057
I am being patched through
right now, sir.

00:19:38.091 --> 00:19:39.285
On screen.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.295
Quark, I see you remember me.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:45.855
How could I forget
the only man ever to win

00:19:45.899 --> 00:19:48.663
triple down dabo
at one of my tables?

00:19:48.702 --> 00:19:50.533
And how can I forget
that you didn't have

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:52.128
enough latinum
to cover my winnings?

00:19:52.172 --> 00:19:53.571
I thought I explained

00:19:53.607 --> 00:19:56.701
that my brother misplaced
the key to the safe.

00:19:56.743 --> 00:19:58.540
Besides,
those vouchers I gave you

00:19:58.578 --> 00:20:00.409
were every bit as good
as latinum.

00:20:00.447 --> 00:20:02.506
You can spend latinum
almost anywhere.

00:20:02.549 --> 00:20:04.449
Those vouchers are
only good at your bar.

00:20:05.585 --> 00:20:09.214
Is, um...
that what this is about?

00:20:09.256 --> 00:20:10.348
You're on your way

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.654
and you're calling to reserve
a holosuite program?

00:20:14.561 --> 00:20:17.724
Actually, I was hoping you could
help me with something else.

00:20:17.764 --> 00:20:19.595
What would that be?

00:20:19.633 --> 00:20:22.602
I'm looking for some Klingon
friends of mine...

00:20:22.636 --> 00:20:25.002
the Duras sisters,
Lursa and B'Etor.

00:20:25.038 --> 00:20:26.869
Yes.

00:20:26.907 --> 00:20:29.467
Lursa and B'Etor.

00:20:29.509 --> 00:20:32.307
Big talk, small tips.

00:20:32.345 --> 00:20:33.903
Do you know
where I can find them?

00:20:35.282 --> 00:20:38.911
Well, I did hear a rumor,
actually.

00:20:38.952 --> 00:20:40.510
What kind of rumor?

00:20:40.554 --> 00:20:41.521
Oh, I don't know.

00:20:41.555 --> 00:20:43.318
I'm sure it was told me
in confidence.

00:20:43.356 --> 00:20:47.315
And how much would
your confidence cost?

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.851
How many vouchers
do you have again?

00:20:49.896 --> 00:20:53.923
I have enough
for 12 bars of latinum.

00:20:55.769 --> 00:20:58.067
I'd be glad to return them.

00:20:58.104 --> 00:20:59.731
I believe the rumor was

00:20:59.773 --> 00:21:02.139
that the sisters were trying
to buy

00:21:02.175 --> 00:21:04.700
some secondhand
mining equipment.

00:21:04.744 --> 00:21:06.439
What for?

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:09.540
They learned of a magnesite
deposit on the Kalla system.

00:21:09.583 --> 00:21:11.073
It belongs to the Pakleds

00:21:11.117 --> 00:21:13.677
but those fools don't even know
it's there.

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:16.211
Your, uh, friends
are trying to get at it.

00:21:16.256 --> 00:21:18.554
All right.

00:21:18.592 --> 00:21:20.890
I'll send those vouchers to you.

00:21:20.961 --> 00:21:23.259
Oh. Don't bother.

00:21:23.296 --> 00:21:26.356
I voided them
while we've been talking.

00:21:26.399 --> 00:21:29.232
So long, Quark.

00:21:32.305 --> 00:21:34.899
How long would it take us
to get to the Kalla system?

00:21:35.008 --> 00:21:36.999
Approximately 16 hours, sir.

00:21:37.043 --> 00:21:38.533
Could not he have been lying?

00:21:38.578 --> 00:21:40.170
Why would he?

00:21:40.213 --> 00:21:43.580
I'd just be knocking
on his door again in a few days

00:21:43.617 --> 00:21:46.177
and I wouldn't be
in as good a mood.

00:21:46.219 --> 00:21:47.880
Uh-huh.

00:21:47.921 --> 00:21:49.786
Congratulations, Commander.

00:21:49.823 --> 00:21:53.020
I did not think it
would be possible

00:21:53.059 --> 00:21:55.152
to find the sisters.

00:21:55.195 --> 00:21:57.026
Take us out of orbit.

00:21:57.063 --> 00:21:58.496
Aye, sir.

00:22:03.069 --> 00:22:06.698
I took the liberty
of creating a holodeck program.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.230
What kind of program?

00:22:08.275 --> 00:22:09.833
I'll show you.

00:22:09.876 --> 00:22:12.436
Computer, run program
K'mtar Alpha-one.

00:22:12.479 --> 00:22:13.878
Program initiated.

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:15.675
Enter when ready.

00:22:22.188 --> 00:22:25.021
Why did you want
to recreate this?

00:22:25.058 --> 00:22:27.253
You said you wished
you had been able

00:22:27.294 --> 00:22:30.889
to help your father fight,
but you did not know how.

00:22:30.997 --> 00:22:33.465
You have probably
fought that battle

00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:35.764
over and over again
in your mind.

00:22:35.802 --> 00:22:37.497
Yes.

00:22:37.537 --> 00:22:40.768
Let's see what happens now.

00:22:40.807 --> 00:22:44.971
Computer, give me
two Klingon warriors!

00:22:46.713 --> 00:22:50.479
How can I fight
someone that big?

00:22:50.517 --> 00:22:53.577
Size is not
the most important thing.

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:56.885
Skill, cunning,
powers of observation

00:22:56.923 --> 00:22:59.483
are the most
important weapons.

00:22:59.526 --> 00:23:01.221
Ni'tokor bak'to!

00:23:14.341 --> 00:23:17.174
Freeze program.

00:23:19.145 --> 00:23:22.205
Look what this ko'tal
is doing, hmm.

00:23:25.585 --> 00:23:27.052
You see his leg?

00:23:27.087 --> 00:23:29.555
That will give you a clue

00:23:29.589 --> 00:23:32.558
as to what his next move
will be.

00:23:32.592 --> 00:23:35.459
All his weight is
on his right foot.

00:23:35.495 --> 00:23:38.396
Yes, he is going to have to
shift it to regain his balance.

00:23:40.967 --> 00:23:42.491
Stand ready!

00:23:43.570 --> 00:23:47.563
Computer, resume program.

00:23:50.443 --> 00:23:52.911
Po'tajg! Po'tajg!

00:23:52.946 --> 00:23:54.846
Finish him.

00:24:06.292 --> 00:24:07.850
Freeze program!

00:24:11.064 --> 00:24:14.500
You should have killed him
when you had the chance.

00:24:14.534 --> 00:24:15.865
Why did you not?

00:24:17.137 --> 00:24:18.729
I don't know.

00:24:18.772 --> 00:24:21.138
Look at him!

00:24:21.174 --> 00:24:23.039
He did not care
that you showed him mercy!

00:24:23.076 --> 00:24:25.874
He was going to kill you!

00:24:25.912 --> 00:24:27.311
K'mtar, that is enough.

00:24:29.082 --> 00:24:32.279
If this was real,
he'd be dead by now.

00:24:34.020 --> 00:24:36.420
Alexander!

00:24:43.263 --> 00:24:44.787
We are approaching Kalla III.

00:24:44.831 --> 00:24:46.128
Set a standard orbit.

00:24:46.166 --> 00:24:48.430
Any evidence
of a mining expedition?

00:24:48.468 --> 00:24:51.096
A shaft has been cut
through the outer crust.

00:24:51.137 --> 00:24:52.695
There is evidence of machinery

00:24:52.739 --> 00:24:54.536
but it does not appear
to be in use.

00:24:54.574 --> 00:24:56.405
Life signs?

00:24:56.443 --> 00:24:58.001
It is difficult to say.

00:24:58.044 --> 00:25:00.979
The magnesite is interfering
with bio-readings.

00:25:01.014 --> 00:25:02.572
Assemble an away team.

00:25:24.604 --> 00:25:26.003
Who are you?

00:25:26.039 --> 00:25:27.529
Gorta.

00:25:27.574 --> 00:25:29.269
I'm Gorta.

00:25:32.912 --> 00:25:35.881
What are you doing
on this planet?

00:25:35.915 --> 00:25:37.507
I crashed here.

00:25:37.550 --> 00:25:40.041
Then you are denying involvement

00:25:40.086 --> 00:25:41.747
in illegal mining activities?

00:25:41.788 --> 00:25:43.050
Mining?

00:25:43.089 --> 00:25:46.889
So, that's what all
this equipment is here for.

00:25:46.926 --> 00:25:49.326
We are looking
for two Klingon women.

00:25:49.362 --> 00:25:50.556
Sisters.

00:25:50.597 --> 00:25:52.064
Lursa? B'Etor?

00:25:52.098 --> 00:25:54.157
Do you know where they are?

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:55.827
Actually, we were hoping
that you did.

00:26:00.607 --> 00:26:02.598
M-Maybe I do.

00:26:02.642 --> 00:26:05.270
Would you be willing to share
your information with us?

00:26:05.311 --> 00:26:09.407
My personal code of conduct
prohibits sharing.

00:26:09.449 --> 00:26:11.508
But I'd consider a trade.

00:26:11.551 --> 00:26:13.951
Does your personal code
of conduct tell you

00:26:13.987 --> 00:26:16.319
that when you're stranded
on a planet with no way off

00:26:16.356 --> 00:26:17.983
you shouldn't try to cut deals?

00:26:18.024 --> 00:26:21.016
You have a point.

00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:24.029
We could certainly provide
passage off this planet

00:26:24.063 --> 00:26:25.860
in exchange for information.

00:26:25.965 --> 00:26:29.492
Could you perhaps
fail to tell the Pakleds

00:26:29.536 --> 00:26:31.231
that we were mining their ore?

00:26:31.271 --> 00:26:32.568
Don't push your luck.

00:26:32.605 --> 00:26:35.631
But if you get us
the Duras sisters

00:26:35.675 --> 00:26:37.700
I'll see what I can do.

00:26:37.744 --> 00:26:40.474
Ahh.

00:26:40.513 --> 00:26:43.539
The Duras sisters.

00:26:43.583 --> 00:26:47.883
They are magnificent,
aren't they?

00:26:47.921 --> 00:26:49.286
Where are they now?

00:26:49.322 --> 00:26:52.223
Selling the ore, I imagine.

00:26:52.258 --> 00:26:55.887
They took everything...
the ore, the ship.

00:26:55.962 --> 00:26:57.395
And where have they gone?

00:26:57.430 --> 00:27:00.422
We were going to sell the ore
to a Yridian trader.

00:27:00.466 --> 00:27:03.697
We were supposed to meet him
in the Ufandi system.

00:27:03.736 --> 00:27:05.465
Gather your belongings.

00:27:05.505 --> 00:27:07.473
It is time to leave.

00:27:12.679 --> 00:27:16.115
Like I said,
they took everything.

00:27:26.425 --> 00:27:27.858
Worf...

00:27:27.926 --> 00:27:30.793
I am sorry about what happened.

00:27:30.829 --> 00:27:33.662
I should not
have gotten so angry.

00:27:33.699 --> 00:27:35.758
It's just that I am...

00:27:35.801 --> 00:27:37.530
worried about Alexander.

00:27:40.672 --> 00:27:42.333
As am I.

00:27:42.374 --> 00:27:46.538
Kurn told me that his mother
actively discouraged him

00:27:46.578 --> 00:27:48.478
exploring his Klingon heritage.

00:27:48.514 --> 00:27:50.880
When he first came
to live with me

00:27:50.983 --> 00:27:53.213
he knew nothing of our ways.

00:27:53.252 --> 00:27:54.879
He often reminds me

00:27:54.920 --> 00:27:58.117
of the things
his mother said to him.

00:27:58.157 --> 00:28:01.058
And I try not
to disregard her wishes.

00:28:01.093 --> 00:28:03.618
I want the boy
to honor his mother.

00:28:03.662 --> 00:28:06.563
Someday I'm sure
he will appreciate you

00:28:06.598 --> 00:28:10.728
and be grateful for all
that you have done for him.

00:28:10.769 --> 00:28:13.533
But still, compared
to other boys his age

00:28:13.572 --> 00:28:17.508
his fighting skills
are years behind.

00:28:17.543 --> 00:28:18.840
Yes, I know.

00:28:18.911 --> 00:28:21.607
He does not put in
the time it takes

00:28:21.647 --> 00:28:22.841
to learn the skills.

00:28:22.881 --> 00:28:24.712
I thought that you
might consider

00:28:24.750 --> 00:28:28.982
sending him to
the Training Academy at Ogat.

00:28:29.021 --> 00:28:31.216
Your brother is
an influential man.

00:28:31.256 --> 00:28:34.851
I'm sure he could see to it
that Alexander was admitted.

00:28:34.960 --> 00:28:36.393
Ogat...

00:28:36.428 --> 00:28:39.693
I am only thinking
of what is best for the boy.

00:28:39.731 --> 00:28:42.165
There he would learn our ways.

00:28:42.201 --> 00:28:44.192
He would live like a Klingon.

00:28:44.236 --> 00:28:47.262
I would like him
to learn our ways.

00:28:49.007 --> 00:28:50.531
No.

00:28:50.576 --> 00:28:53.511
This is his home.

00:28:56.481 --> 00:29:00.417
How can you expect him
to lead our family

00:29:00.452 --> 00:29:02.647
when all he knows is life

00:29:02.688 --> 00:29:04.952
aboard a Federation starship?

00:29:04.990 --> 00:29:06.457
He is my son.

00:29:06.491 --> 00:29:08.356
He belongs with me.

00:29:08.393 --> 00:29:10.827
The boy is
more human than Klingon.

00:29:10.862 --> 00:29:13.797
If he stays here,
he will never be a warrior.

00:29:13.832 --> 00:29:15.390
He will never be able

00:29:15.434 --> 00:29:17.459
to defend our family
against its enemies!

00:29:17.502 --> 00:29:18.526
Enough! Enough!

00:29:18.570 --> 00:29:20.265
Enough! The decision is mine!

00:29:20.305 --> 00:29:21.772
Not necessarily.

00:29:21.807 --> 00:29:25.265
I would be well within my rights
to invoke ya'nora kor.

00:29:25.310 --> 00:29:29.178
You would question my fitness
to raise my own son?

00:29:29.214 --> 00:29:31.011
For the good of our house

00:29:31.049 --> 00:29:33.040
yes, Worf.

00:29:33.085 --> 00:29:34.575
I beg of you.

00:29:34.620 --> 00:29:37.248
Please stop thinking
of yourself.

00:29:37.289 --> 00:29:40.554
It is Alexander
we should be considering.

00:29:40.592 --> 00:29:43.220
Look into your heart

00:29:43.262 --> 00:29:46.527
and do what is best for him.

00:29:57.609 --> 00:30:01.978
Kahless was determined
to teach his brother a lesson

00:30:02.014 --> 00:30:04.881
because he had told a lie.

00:30:04.983 --> 00:30:07.543
But Morath refused to fight him

00:30:07.586 --> 00:30:09.816
and instead ran away.

00:30:09.855 --> 00:30:12.346
Kahless pursued him
across the valleys

00:30:12.391 --> 00:30:16.487
over the mountains
and down to the edge of the sea.

00:30:16.528 --> 00:30:19.361
And there, at the shore,
they fought for 12...

00:30:19.398 --> 00:30:20.797
12 days, 12 nights.

00:30:20.832 --> 00:30:22.891
I know.
I've heard this story before.

00:30:23.001 --> 00:30:24.662
Hmm.

00:30:24.703 --> 00:30:28.400
Alexander, it is important
to tell these stories

00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:31.000
even though we
already know them.

00:30:31.043 --> 00:30:33.705
Well, why was Kahless so mad
about the lie

00:30:33.745 --> 00:30:34.905
his brother told?

00:30:34.946 --> 00:30:36.573
It made him look like a coward.

00:30:36.615 --> 00:30:39.015
If Kahless would have just
explained what happened

00:30:39.051 --> 00:30:41.349
maybe they wouldn't
have had to fight about it.

00:30:41.386 --> 00:30:42.910
You're missing the point.

00:30:42.954 --> 00:30:45.184
Why was it so wrong
for Morath to run away?

00:30:45.223 --> 00:30:47.623
Maybe he didn't want
to fight his brother

00:30:47.659 --> 00:30:49.889
because he didn't want
to have to kill him.

00:30:49.928 --> 00:30:52.726
He ran because he was a coward.

00:30:52.764 --> 00:30:54.129
But how do you know th...?

00:30:54.166 --> 00:30:55.724
No, no, no, no.
No more questions.

00:30:55.767 --> 00:30:58.395
These are our stories.

00:30:58.437 --> 00:31:00.837
It is important
for a warrior to learn

00:31:00.872 --> 00:31:03.602
how to interpret them properly.

00:31:03.642 --> 00:31:04.870
I'm trying to.

00:31:04.943 --> 00:31:09.141
No, your head is filled
with foolish human notions

00:31:09.181 --> 00:31:10.978
about how things are.

00:31:11.016 --> 00:31:12.711
You are Klingon!

00:31:12.751 --> 00:31:16.551
It is time you began
to act like one.

00:31:16.588 --> 00:31:19.113
I am part human, too.

00:31:19.157 --> 00:31:21.648
Listen to me, Alexander.

00:31:21.693 --> 00:31:25.857
When a human looks at you,
he does not see himself.

00:31:25.897 --> 00:31:27.421
He sees a Klingon.

00:31:27.466 --> 00:31:29.730
It doesn't matter
what I look like.

00:31:29.768 --> 00:31:31.292
It does.

00:31:31.336 --> 00:31:34.772
You are different than everyone
else aboard this ship.

00:31:34.806 --> 00:31:35.864
That's not true!

00:31:35.907 --> 00:31:37.101
It is.

00:31:37.142 --> 00:31:41.772
The only way that you will ever
feel as if you truly belong

00:31:41.813 --> 00:31:47.046
is to leave here, and go
and live with your own kind.

00:31:55.494 --> 00:31:58.657
I know a Klingon school
you could go to.

00:31:58.697 --> 00:32:01.131
Oh, you would be welcome there.

00:32:01.166 --> 00:32:04.135
They would teach you
to be a warrior...

00:32:04.169 --> 00:32:06.797
prepare you
for the Rite of Ascension.

00:32:06.838 --> 00:32:09.033
I don't know
if I want to do that.

00:32:09.074 --> 00:32:12.202
After you were there for a while

00:32:12.244 --> 00:32:16.203
you would find that you wouldn't
want to do anything else.

00:32:16.248 --> 00:32:18.079
I don't want to leave
the Enterprise.

00:32:18.116 --> 00:32:19.777
Alexander, you must!

00:32:19.818 --> 00:32:22.651
Everything depends upon it!

00:32:22.687 --> 00:32:25.212
I thought you were different.

00:32:27.359 --> 00:32:32.319
I thought you understood me,
but you don't.

00:32:32.364 --> 00:32:33.592
You're just like my father.

00:32:33.632 --> 00:32:36.567
All you care about
is me becoming a warrior.

00:32:36.601 --> 00:32:38.466
Just leave me alone!

00:32:42.808 --> 00:32:47.006
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 47779.4.

00:32:47.045 --> 00:32:49.240
We've entered the Ufandi system

00:32:49.281 --> 00:32:51.647
where we believe
the Duras sisters

00:32:51.683 --> 00:32:55.676
might have come to sell the ore
they mined on Kalla III.

00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:59.656
I am detecting a vessel holding
position near the third planet.

00:32:59.691 --> 00:33:01.158
It is a Yridian freighter.

00:33:01.193 --> 00:33:02.558
Put it on screen.

00:33:04.162 --> 00:33:06.289
Scan for magnesite in its hold.

00:33:08.099 --> 00:33:10.397
The resonance signature
indicates

00:33:10.435 --> 00:33:12.869
that there is
magnesite ore present.

00:33:12.938 --> 00:33:14.428
Then we're too late.

00:33:14.473 --> 00:33:16.464
The sisters have
already been here.

00:33:16.508 --> 00:33:19.306
Somehow, I doubt the Yridians
are going to be forthcoming

00:33:19.344 --> 00:33:20.868
about where they
might have gone.

00:33:20.979 --> 00:33:22.139
Sir, readings

00:33:22.180 --> 00:33:24.375
indicate that there
are only 500 kilograms

00:33:24.416 --> 00:33:26.680
of ore in the Yridian hold.

00:33:26.718 --> 00:33:28.686
There should be
over 10,000 kilograms.

00:33:28.720 --> 00:33:29.880
That's odd.

00:33:29.955 --> 00:33:31.286
Hail them.

00:33:31.323 --> 00:33:33.484
I'm Commander William Riker

00:33:33.525 --> 00:33:36.358
from the Federation
Starship Enterprise.

00:33:36.394 --> 00:33:37.861
I am Yog.

00:33:37.896 --> 00:33:39.659
Why are we speaking?

00:33:39.698 --> 00:33:41.461
Our sensors indicate

00:33:41.500 --> 00:33:43.491
that you're carrying
magnesite ore.

00:33:43.535 --> 00:33:45.833
Magnesite. Yes.

00:33:45.871 --> 00:33:47.168
Where did you get it?

00:33:47.205 --> 00:33:48.832
From a Corvallan.

00:33:48.874 --> 00:33:51.240
For a good price.

00:33:51.276 --> 00:33:53.642
Where is this Corvallan now?

00:33:53.678 --> 00:33:56.738
I'm under orders
to acquire some magnesite.

00:33:56.781 --> 00:33:58.248
Well, he is gone.

00:33:58.283 --> 00:34:00.114
Where?

00:34:00.151 --> 00:34:01.641
Who is to know?

00:34:01.686 --> 00:34:03.517
Would you be interested
in selling me

00:34:03.555 --> 00:34:05.045
the ore that you're carrying?

00:34:05.090 --> 00:34:06.387
No.

00:34:06.424 --> 00:34:09.018
I have a buyer.

00:34:09.060 --> 00:34:12.393
You haven't heard my offer.

00:34:12.430 --> 00:34:16.628
Half a gram
of Anjoran biomimetic gel.

00:34:16.668 --> 00:34:18.602
Hmm.

00:34:18.637 --> 00:34:20.264
Done.

00:34:21.973 --> 00:34:24.669
Once we verify the purity
of your ore

00:34:24.709 --> 00:34:26.540
we'll beam over the gel.

00:34:29.147 --> 00:34:31.240
You're up to something.

00:34:31.283 --> 00:34:35.344
Have the transporter room beam
the ore to these coordinates.

00:34:35.387 --> 00:34:36.877
Sir?

00:34:36.922 --> 00:34:38.014
That would place the ore

00:34:38.056 --> 00:34:39.751
directly off
the ship's starboard bow.

00:34:39.791 --> 00:34:41.418
I know.

00:34:44.162 --> 00:34:46.289
Transport complete.

00:34:46.331 --> 00:34:49.323
Lock the phasers
on the ore and fire.

00:34:49.367 --> 00:34:51.358
Firing.

00:34:53.371 --> 00:34:55.566
A Klingon bird-of-prey.

00:34:55.607 --> 00:34:56.904
Put a tractor beam on it.

00:34:56.942 --> 00:34:58.136
How did you know?

00:34:58.176 --> 00:35:00.736
The Yridians had only part
of the shipment in their hold.

00:35:00.779 --> 00:35:02.144
I realized that we had arrived

00:35:02.180 --> 00:35:03.943
before they had completed
the transfer.

00:35:03.982 --> 00:35:05.847
The Klingon ship is hailing us.

00:35:05.884 --> 00:35:07.215
On screen.

00:35:09.020 --> 00:35:10.817
Release our vessel at once!

00:35:10.855 --> 00:35:11.981
I don't think so.

00:35:12.023 --> 00:35:13.320
We've done nothing wrong.

00:35:13.358 --> 00:35:16.725
We were engaging in a simple
business transaction.

00:35:18.663 --> 00:35:21.257
We know you're dealing
in stolen ore

00:35:21.299 --> 00:35:24.097
but I want to talk
about the assassination attempt

00:35:24.135 --> 00:35:25.500
on Lieutenant Worf.

00:35:25.537 --> 00:35:27.630
What assassination attempt?

00:35:27.672 --> 00:35:30.106
This is the first
I've heard of it.

00:35:30.141 --> 00:35:31.768
Too bad it didn't succeed!

00:35:31.810 --> 00:35:32.799
Ha!

00:35:34.312 --> 00:35:36.303
We have evidence
that you're behind it.

00:35:36.348 --> 00:35:38.475
That is outrageous!

00:35:38.516 --> 00:35:40.484
What is this evidence?

00:35:40.518 --> 00:35:41.883
Beam over.

00:35:41.987 --> 00:35:43.511
We'll show you.

00:35:44.856 --> 00:35:48.660
We'll be there... shortly.

00:35:52.897 --> 00:35:56.526
This was dropped
by one of the assassins.

00:35:57.869 --> 00:35:59.996
It bears the crest
of your house.

00:36:00.038 --> 00:36:01.596
Ge'ko... kaf'la.

00:36:01.639 --> 00:36:04.472
Someone must have given
it to the assassins

00:36:04.509 --> 00:36:06.340
to implicate us.

00:36:06.377 --> 00:36:08.208
Why would someone do that?

00:36:08.246 --> 00:36:11.647
In order
to tarnish our good name.

00:36:11.683 --> 00:36:14.083
You cannot tarnish
a rusted blade.

00:36:14.118 --> 00:36:16.018
Ji'ko to'val!

00:36:16.054 --> 00:36:17.112
Gir'nak tovo'sor!

00:36:17.155 --> 00:36:18.452
Mr. Worf!

00:36:18.489 --> 00:36:20.457
You said there was
other evidence

00:36:20.491 --> 00:36:21.958
that they were involved?

00:36:21.993 --> 00:36:23.654
Yes. On the Homeworld.

00:36:23.695 --> 00:36:26.357
We'll set a course.
I want this thing cleared up.

00:36:28.299 --> 00:36:30.699
I will send a message to Kurn.

00:36:30.735 --> 00:36:33.966
He may wish to return
to the Homeworld, as well.

00:36:34.005 --> 00:36:36.098
Bet'ala nog'tor.

00:36:38.409 --> 00:36:40.070
Impossible.

00:36:42.246 --> 00:36:43.713
What is it?

00:36:43.748 --> 00:36:47.115
These markings represent
the members of our house.

00:36:47.151 --> 00:36:48.880
This symbol represents

00:36:48.953 --> 00:36:52.514
our father, myself, my sister

00:36:52.557 --> 00:36:54.184
and this...

00:36:54.225 --> 00:36:57.888
represents her son.

00:36:57.995 --> 00:37:00.122
I was not aware you had a son.

00:37:00.164 --> 00:37:03.292
I do not.

00:37:03.334 --> 00:37:06.064
But I am with child.

00:37:06.104 --> 00:37:09.073
She found out
only a few days ago

00:37:09.107 --> 00:37:11.405
and told no one but me.

00:37:11.442 --> 00:37:14.240
How can this marking be here?!

00:37:14.278 --> 00:37:16.712
Where did this come from?

00:37:20.318 --> 00:37:23.754
I will speak with K'mtar.

00:37:49.180 --> 00:37:51.148
Father...

00:37:51.182 --> 00:37:52.376
stop!

00:37:52.416 --> 00:37:54.043
I am your son.

00:37:54.085 --> 00:37:58.681
I am Alexander.

00:38:05.963 --> 00:38:07.954
What are you saying?

00:38:07.998 --> 00:38:10.193
I am your son, Alexander.

00:38:10.234 --> 00:38:14.568
I have come to this time
from 40 years in the future.

00:38:14.605 --> 00:38:16.835
P'tak. Tell me the truth

00:38:16.874 --> 00:38:18.705
or I will kill you.

00:38:18.742 --> 00:38:20.073
Look at me.

00:38:20.110 --> 00:38:23.773
When we first met,
you said I looked familiar.

00:38:23.814 --> 00:38:25.372
I could have seen you
on the Homeworld.

00:38:25.415 --> 00:38:26.507
No!

00:38:26.550 --> 00:38:27.847
Look closely.

00:38:27.951 --> 00:38:30.852
I am your son.

00:38:30.954 --> 00:38:34.617
If you are Alexander,
you will remember

00:38:34.658 --> 00:38:38.526
your mother's last words
before she died.

00:38:38.562 --> 00:38:43.226
I was three years old.

00:38:43.267 --> 00:38:45.792
She was dying when we found her.

00:38:45.836 --> 00:38:49.966
She barely managed
to whisper my name

00:38:50.007 --> 00:38:55.274
and then she took my hand
and placed it in yours.

00:38:55.312 --> 00:38:56.745
Then she died

00:38:56.780 --> 00:39:00.375
and then you howled in rage

00:39:00.417 --> 00:39:03.580
and said, "Look upon her.

00:39:03.620 --> 00:39:08.182
"Look upon death
and always remember."

00:39:08.225 --> 00:39:10.489
And I always have.

00:39:18.335 --> 00:39:20.929
How have you done this...

00:39:20.971 --> 00:39:22.939
come to this time?

00:39:22.973 --> 00:39:26.500
I met a man
in the Cambra system.

00:39:26.543 --> 00:39:29.944
He gave me a chance
to change the past.

00:39:29.980 --> 00:39:33.711
He had the ability
to send me here to this time.

00:39:33.750 --> 00:39:36.742
And you came here
in order to end your own life.

00:39:36.787 --> 00:39:39.585
I was hoping
that I would not have to...

00:39:39.623 --> 00:39:43.354
that I could change things,
that I could change myself.

00:39:43.393 --> 00:39:46.089
But I could not

00:39:46.129 --> 00:39:51.328
and now everything is going
to turn out like it did before.

00:39:51.368 --> 00:39:54.132
I cannot let that happen.

00:39:54.171 --> 00:39:57.470
But why? What is going to happen
that is so terrible?

00:39:57.507 --> 00:39:59.668
You will be killed

00:39:59.710 --> 00:40:02.406
because I was too naive

00:40:02.446 --> 00:40:05.609
too weak to be able
to protect you.

00:40:05.649 --> 00:40:08.880
I do not believe that.

00:40:08.919 --> 00:40:10.181
I was there.

00:40:10.220 --> 00:40:12.017
I saw you murdered.

00:40:12.055 --> 00:40:14.046
I was to blame.

00:40:17.027 --> 00:40:19.621
You must not blame yourself.

00:40:19.663 --> 00:40:21.756
You don't understand.

00:40:21.798 --> 00:40:26.292
I did not become a warrior.

00:40:26.336 --> 00:40:27.860
I was a...

00:40:27.904 --> 00:40:30.498
a diplomat, a peacemaker.

00:40:30.540 --> 00:40:33.270
When it came my time
to lead our family

00:40:33.310 --> 00:40:36.768
I thought that I could
single-handedly end the fighting

00:40:36.813 --> 00:40:38.838
between the great houses.

00:40:38.882 --> 00:40:41.908
I publicly announced
that the House of Mogh

00:40:41.952 --> 00:40:44.546
would be the first
to end the feuding

00:40:44.588 --> 00:40:48.684
that there would be no more
retribution, no more revenge.

00:40:48.725 --> 00:40:50.192
You tried to warn me.

00:40:50.227 --> 00:40:54.095
You tried to tell me
that I should not show weakness

00:40:54.131 --> 00:40:57.100
but I thought you were
a foolish old man.

00:40:57.134 --> 00:41:01.093
I told you you were a relic
from an earlier time

00:41:01.138 --> 00:41:04.437
and that a new era of peace
was at hand.

00:41:04.474 --> 00:41:06.101
But you were right.

00:41:06.143 --> 00:41:11.274
My enemies saw my weakness
and moved against me.

00:41:11.314 --> 00:41:14.681
And unless I stop it right now

00:41:14.718 --> 00:41:18.586
that boy will see
his father killed on the floor

00:41:18.622 --> 00:41:20.590
of the Great Council Chamber.

00:41:20.624 --> 00:41:23.650
Ah, that is why you wanted
to take Alexander away...

00:41:23.693 --> 00:41:25.558
to turn him into a warrior.

00:41:25.595 --> 00:41:28.155
I staged
the assassination attempt

00:41:28.198 --> 00:41:31.258
to try and frighten him,
to make him realize

00:41:31.301 --> 00:41:34.361
that he must follow
the ways of a warrior.

00:41:34.404 --> 00:41:36.702
If I had listened to you...

00:41:36.740 --> 00:41:41.507
if I had become the warrior
that you had wanted me to be...

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:47.916
you would not have died
in my arms.

00:41:47.951 --> 00:41:49.145
No.

00:41:49.186 --> 00:41:51.017
Who knows
what the future will be

00:41:51.054 --> 00:41:53.454
now that you have
disrupted time?

00:41:53.490 --> 00:41:54.923
I may die tomorrow

00:41:54.991 --> 00:41:56.925
or I may outlive you.

00:41:56.960 --> 00:41:58.257
But when I die

00:41:58.295 --> 00:42:00.593
I would like an honorable death

00:42:00.630 --> 00:42:03.064
and the only way
that is possible

00:42:03.100 --> 00:42:06.126
is for you to accept
yourself as you are

00:42:06.169 --> 00:42:08.729
and stay true
to what you believe.

00:42:08.772 --> 00:42:11.434
The cause of peace
is a just cause.

00:42:11.475 --> 00:42:14.000
The struggle must continue.

00:42:14.044 --> 00:42:15.875
It is a futile struggle.

00:42:15.946 --> 00:42:17.880
I cannot change things.

00:42:17.948 --> 00:42:21.440
You have already changed things
more than you realize.

00:42:21.485 --> 00:42:24.784
The boy I was has not changed.

00:42:24.821 --> 00:42:27.119
But I have.

00:42:27.157 --> 00:42:31.617
You have given me
a glimpse into my son's future

00:42:31.661 --> 00:42:36.462
and I know now
that he has his own destiny.

00:42:39.302 --> 00:42:42.601
And I believe it
will be a great one.

00:42:49.079 --> 00:42:52.515
I love you, Father.

00:42:52.549 --> 00:42:57.248
And I you, Alexander.

00:43:21.178 --> 00:43:23.169
I have been waiting.

00:43:23.213 --> 00:43:24.703
Where is K'mtar?

00:43:24.748 --> 00:43:26.409
He had to leave.

00:43:26.449 --> 00:43:28.417
He was called away.

00:43:28.451 --> 00:43:31.386
He never said good-bye.

00:43:31.421 --> 00:43:33.685
He asked me
to say good-bye for him.

00:43:33.723 --> 00:43:37.056
He also wanted me to tell you,
no matter what happens

00:43:37.093 --> 00:43:40.062
no matter what you decide
to do with your life

00:43:40.096 --> 00:43:42.724
he will always care for you
a great deal.

00:43:42.766 --> 00:43:44.996
When will I see him again?

00:43:45.035 --> 00:43:49.267
It may be a long time.

00:43:49.306 --> 00:43:53.470
Well, we should start practice.

00:43:53.510 --> 00:43:55.910
Alexander...

00:43:56.012 --> 00:44:00.449
there will be plenty
of time for training.
